      "text": "To convert a point from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we use the following formulas:\n\n$x = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\cos(\\theta)$\n$y = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\sin(\\theta)$\n$z = \\rho \\cos(\\phi)$\n\nIn this case, $\\rho = 3$, $\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}$, and $\\phi = 0$.\n\nUsing the formulas above, we get:\n$x = 3 \\sin(0) \\cos(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}) = 0$\n$y = 3 \\sin(0) \\sin(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}) = 0$\n$z = 3 \\cos(0) = 3$\n\nSo, the rectangular coordinates of the point $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$ are $\\boxed{(0,0,3)}$.The answer is: 0,0,3",
