      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)$ to rectangular coordinates $(x, y, z)$, we use the following relationships:\n\n$$\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta \\\\\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta \\\\\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n$$\n\nGiven spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \nx &= 3 \\sin 0 \\cos \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0 \\\\\ny &= 3 \\sin 0 \\sin \\frac{5\\pi}{12} = 0 \\\\\nz &= 3 \\cos 0 = 3 \n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the rectangular coordinates are $\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}$.",
